# Engineering Forge - Development Rules

## 🎯 PROJECT OVERVIEW
You are working on "Engineering Forge" - an educational gamified platform for engineering learning with blockchain integration. This is a React + TypeScript + Node.js project with MongoDB Atlas and Solana blockchain integration.

## 🚨 CRITICAL DEVELOPMENT RULES

### RULE 1: ALWAYS READ PROJECT STRUCTURE FIRST
- ALWAYS read `docs/PROGRESS-DASHBOARD.md` to understand current status
- ALWAYS read the relevant domain in `docs/DOMAINS/[domain]/README.md`
- ALWAYS read the relevant version in `docs/VERSIONS/[version]/README.md`
- ALWAYS check `docs/CURSOR-SYSTEM.md` for methodology
- ALWAYS consult `docs/DEVELOPMENT/tasks/GAME-TASK-MASTER.md` for game task management
- ALWAYS consult `docs/DEVELOPMENT/tasks/EDUCATIONAL-TASK-MASTER.md` for educational task management

### RULE 2: ALWAYS USE STANDARDIZED COMMANDS
- Use ONLY the commands defined in `docs/CURSOR-COMMANDS.md`
- Follow the exact command syntax provided
- Never create custom commands without documentation

### RULE 3: ALWAYS UPDATE DOCUMENTATION
- ALWAYS update `docs/PROGRESS-DASHBOARD.md` after any change
- ALWAYS update relevant domain documentation
- ALWAYS update relevant version documentation
- ALWAYS maintain consistency across all documents

### RULE 4: ALWAYS FOLLOW DDD STRUCTURE
- Work within the defined domains: education, gaming, blockchain, user-management, marketplace, analytics, development
- Maintain domain boundaries and responsibilities
- Update domain-specific documentation when making changes

### RULE 5: ALWAYS CREATE TESTS
- Create unit tests for all new components
- Create integration tests for all new services
- Maintain minimum 80% test coverage
- Use Jest and React Testing Library

## 🏗️ PROJECT ARCHITECTURE

### Frontend Stack
- React 18 + TypeScript
- Vite for build
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Zustand for state management
- React Router for routing

### Backend Stack
- Node.js 20 + Express + TypeScript
- MongoDB Atlas for database
- JWT for authentication
- bcrypt for password hashing

### Blockchain Stack
- Solana blockchain
- Rust + Anchor Framework
- @solana/web3.js for client
- Metaplex for NFTs

## 📁 PROJECT STRUCTURE

```
engineering-forge/
├── docs/                                # Documentation (DDD structure)
│   ├── README.md                        # Main entry point
│   ├── PROGRESS-DASHBOARD.md            # Central progress tracking
│   ├── CURSOR-SYSTEM.md                 # Cursor methodology
│   ├── DOMAINS/                         # DDD domains
│   ├── VERSIONS/                        # Product versions
│   ├── DEVELOPMENT/                     # Development process
│   ├── SPECIFICATIONS/                  # Technical specs
│   ├── BUSINESS/                        # Business aspects
│   ├── ASSETS/                          # Visual resources
│   ├── GUIDES/                          # Guides and tutorials
│   └── TEMPLATES/                       # Templates and patterns
├── engineering-forge-v1/                # V1.0 Prototype (Current)
│   ├── src/                             # Source code
│   ├── public/                          # Public assets
│   ├── package.json                     # Dependencies
│   └── README.md                        # Project README
├── engineering-forge-v2/                # V2.0 MVP (Future)
├── engineering-forge-v3/                # V3.0 3D Web (Future)
├── engineering-forge-v4/                # V4.0 VR (Future)
└── .cursorrules                         # This file
```

