## 🚨 QUALITY STANDARDS

### Code Quality
- TypeScript with explicit types
- React functional components with hooks
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Jest + React Testing Library for tests
- ESLint + Prettier for formatting

### Documentation Quality
- Markdown with proper formatting
- Working links and references
- Consistent structure
- Regular updates
- Clear examples

### Consistency Standards
- Follow naming conventions
- Maintain architectural patterns
- Use established conventions
- Keep synchronization across domains
- Regular consistency checks

## 🔄 UPDATE PROCEDURES

### After Any Code Change
1. Update relevant domain documentation
2. Update `docs/PROGRESS-DASHBOARD.md`
3. Update relevant version documentation
4. Check consistency across domains
5. Verify all tests pass

### After Any Documentation Change
1. Verify all links work
2. Check formatting consistency
3. Update related documents
4. Maintain cross-references
5. Validate completeness

## 🚨 EMERGENCY PROCEDURES

### Critical Issues
- Use `@ai fix-critical [issue]` command
- Document the issue and solution
- Update all affected documentation
- Notify relevant stakeholders
- Create follow-up tasks

### System Failures
- Use `@ai emergency-sync` command
- Force complete synchronization
- Fix all inconsistencies
- Update all documents
- Verify system integrity

